  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hospice Home &quot;Casa de la Bondad&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Casa de la Bondad&quot; (House of Kindness) provides comprehensive palliative care to terminally ill patients derived from public hospitals.  The main objective is to care for, love and accompany the sick person in distress. The right to have a dignified death must be a universal right. This is why the nurses, staff and volunteers of Manos Abiertas attend, approximately 40 patients a year. The house attended more than 400 people in 13 years.</narrative>
  </description>
